RM(1)                       User Commands

NAME
    rm - remove files

SYNOPSIS
    rm [-df] file...

DESCRIPTION
    rm removes each named file. -d also removes empty directories, and -f
    stays silent about names that do not exist. A symbolic link is
    removed itself; the file or directory it leads to is kept. rm has no
    recursive mode.

SEE ALSO
    ln(1), cp(1), find(1)
